 of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337276/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1059ab6-d512-537f-be1e-28aa492a6ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337278/selection/c5f7ad4aac21b3b2132a0aac4e0a9c58df9e3dc147c764d68867830d09f400b6" :answer/id #uuid "fe062085-7db9-5a01-8166-ecc75fb513dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337278/selection/64a7d10ad15ee0a1bf8938440df4f85252879854dc77c859ae2611c2a4a43dab" :answer/id #uuid "36ffded6-ee5e-5e1f-8d0e-a89f6c288b8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337278/selection/dde0bf389d957fd631eef608bf46a021f5d0660f339d2ec4393a93b040469c86" :answer/id #uuid "56192755-24a1-54b2-bbe6-36fa4a18e2f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337278/selection/b2c1b97d81d20bbe449782d7664d027975c0553720ca36e23c4b2dca8bfbf6ad" :answer/id #uuid "c7bb1a00-6ee8-541c-9610-7657d273bdf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :ans