arying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1059ab6-d512-537f-be1e-28aa492a6ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection/700fc8400a20981acf74206d0716e877f38cb87d56127744097f24bd9f86d4f3" :answer/id #uuid "3bae8f30-a9b1-523b-8750-02bee38eec87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection/dde0bf389d957fd631eef608bf46a021f5d0660f339d2ec4393a93b040469c86" :answer/id #uuid "d7d090ca-b096-54c3-97a4-0221e7d1f597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection/6709e2fcd44460195807ee72441459c60304e1698fd70c8389cae623cedf1a41" :answer/id #uuid "af088a40-016c-57be-a1ca-8a647c105b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection/f44ae1fc5ae371077d9bbe1542727db63dbbf0233cd8b95c2d5c2f05efba53f1" :answer/id #uuid "cd750656-25d0-52a3-a735-98ca4eab9ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection/cba39bfce29c4a78fce11bb0fdfb9fdc3d6b73dd22aa3006c5da520a4b99fc90" :answer/id #uuid "8ecf2147-42c8-5d9d-ad60-389fe599b6b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7e8a7d9-bc76-5e2f-ab40-b8c6ee312d81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337274/selection/cba39bfce29c4a78fce11bb0fdfb9fdc3d6b73dd22aa3006c5da520a4b99fc90" :answer-field/choices ["q-337274/selection/700fc8400a20981acf74206d0716e877f38cb87d56127744097f24bd9f86d4f3" "q-337274/selection/dde0bf389d957fd631eef608bf46a021f5d0660f339d2ec4393a93b040469c86" "q-337274/selection/6709e2fcd44460195807ee72441459c60304e1698fd70c8389cae623cedf1a41" "q-337274/selection/f44ae1fc5ae371077d9bbe1542727db63dbbf0233cd8b95c2d5c2f05efba53f1" "q-337274/selection/cba39bfce29c4a78fce11bb0fdfb9fdc3d6b73dd22aa3006c5da520a4b99fc90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337274" :question/id #uuid "38ecf25c-c9d5-534a-b7ae-492cd6b26809" :question/math-academy-id "q-337274" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, which of the following is a suitable ansatz for the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f