ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352891/field-3/08a62a11362f642ac6e2d448f642099e586336bbdbde83f570899f9bf44e60b0" :answer/id #uuid "6f43e954-574e-502a-877c-4c16ada55b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352891/field-3/a8bc774a9888e48e267545a845f8e7b7a1f8882d72802834f2922f0d992262df" :answer/id #uuid "1b2c773e-9533-5140-9fb2-b5794668210f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352891/field-3/dbcbc0dcb0853eacee9bc4f06f45065e951d48aac90bf93eab85553e04ef79b7" :answer/id #uuid "586f09db-6b5e-578a-81e5-54426aaa5c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352891/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2395c858-1801-51a8-9656-5294ed8b6cd6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-352891/field-3/4d6319dc0dc75df209c5b238bfbc2fb03814a8c96f77aa9f196e030c0453e19f" :answer-field/choices ["q-352891/field-3/4d6319dc0dc75df209c5b238bfbc2fb03814a8c96f77aa9f196e030c0453e19f" "q-352891/field-3/8c000a7f3c58709afb1b27783fb11961224e14eb25b4b5dfa431ec27e0d95da4" "q-352891/field-3/08a62a11362f642ac6e2d448f642099e586336bbdbde83f570899f9bf44e60b0" "q-352891/field-3/a8bc774a9888e48e267545a845f8e7b7a1f8882d72802834f2922f0d992262df" "q-352891/field-3/dbcbc0dcb0853eacee9bc4f06f45065e951d48aac90bf93eab85553e04ef79b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352891" :question/id #uuid "94c1a434-d90c-5a8b-b10b-a3af3883d298" :question/math-academy-id "q-352891" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=6{e}^{-5x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-2x})}^{′}+2(u{e}^{-2x}) & =6{e}^{-5x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-2u{e}^{-2x}+2u{e}^{-2x} & =6{e}^{-5x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}}+\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}} & =6{e}^{-5x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x} & =6{e}^{-5x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =-2{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-2x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352891/field-1" "q-352891/field-2" "q-352891/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1/1be23322a705239834ee3034ce66e7e2d3abe104c3198062f03111fa44fff1d8" :answer/id #uuid "39c33438-9102-5aac-8846-8bae71eca5fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1/90244fea567263d29a122e974f426c797e64ce018b292ff9ad249e079209d91d" :answer/id #uuid "4beb7f87-00b7-5e9f-ba45-e98171b40d16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1/58e66e13dc98313f1c71e73a32f04479429e770bf3852598ea62e9f4fbb454e6" :answer/id #uuid "54d88ef0-316a-5bd7-ad34-6fd868dc1d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1/0f0bf3e5b4d49d098cc5baf660c6977edc9ec113af6f735d59f497de50943951" :answer/id #uuid "53382c9c-8a39-5fd7-aad0-552180ad4298" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1/d2e81689053b2ebae446faeee3737f8c65f277d7870bb0a42ccc7852d3d0d24d" :answer/id #uuid "bf41dca0-2d07-5362-ad81-c525b027914e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352890/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3caac505-b71f-59b4-9208-cd6f0956283c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-352890/field-1/1be23322a705239834ee3034ce66e7e2d3abe104c3198062f03111fa44fff1d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-352890/field-1/1be23322a705239834ee3034ce66e7e2d3abe104c3198062f03111fa44fff1d8" "q-352890/field-1/90244fea567263d29a122e974f426c797e64ce018b292ff9ad249e079209d91d" "q-352890/field-1/58e66e13dc98313f1c71e73a32f04479429e770bf3852598ea62e9f4fbb454e6" "q-352890/field-1/0f0bf3e5b4d49d098cc5baf660c6977edc9ec113af6f735d59f497de50943951" "q-352890/field-1/d2e81689053b2ebae446faeee3737f8c65f277d7870bb0a42ccc7852d3d0d24d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:d